     "input": {
      "summary": "Since about 02:14 UTC, p95 latency on orders has been around 4.2s, and some GET /orders/{id} requests fail after 30s. The service's Hikari database connection pool is full: 20 of 20 connections busy, none free, 212 requests waiting. The database queries themselves stay fast (7ms p95). The pool filled right after a large report export began at 02:12:30, and the export logs that it holds a connection while it streams.",
      "root_cause": "The orders service's database connection pool (HikariPool-1, maximum 20 connections) ran out. Requests wait in pool.acquire (p95 4.15s) and time out after 30s. Postgres is not slow: SELECT orders p95 is 7ms. The most likely trigger is the report export started at 02:12:30 (\"14000 orders, holding connection for streaming\"), which keeps connections checked out for a long time. One gap remains: I could not see how many connections the export takes, and one connection alone would not fill a pool of 20.",
      "confidence": 0.55,
      "evidence": [
       {
        "id": "ev5",
        "claim": "Orders logged 'HikariPool-1 stats (total=20, active=20, idle=0, waiting=212)' 40 times and 'Connection is not available, request timed out after 30000ms' 60 times."
       },
       {
        "id": "ev4",
        "claim": "Since 02:10, pool.acquire p95 is 4.15s, GET /orders/{id} p95 is 30.005s (the timeout), and SELECT orders p95 is only 7ms. The time goes to waiting for a connection, not to the database."
       },
       {
        "id": "ev7",
        "claim": "A sample failing request at 02:25:12 took 30005ms, with status 'Connection is not available, request timed out after 30000ms'."
       },
       {
        "id": "ev13",
        "claim": "At 02:12:30, 1.5 minutes before the alert, orders logged 'report export started: 14000 orders, holding connection for streaming'."
       },
       {
        "id": "ev12",
        "claim": "Between 01:50 and 02:20 the export is the only orders log line that is not a pool error."
       },
       {
        "id": "ev2",
        "claim": "No deploy was recorded and no version change was seen in the past day."
       },
       {
        "id": "ev1",
        "claim": "Inventory is healthy (p95 25ms, 0% errors). The api-gateway p95 of 4.1s reflects the slow orders responses."
       }
      ],
      "ruled_out": [
       "A deploy or new version: none recorded and no new version seen (ev2, ev3).",
       "Slow Postgres queries: SELECT orders p95 stays at 7ms while pool.acquire waits seconds (ev4).",
       "Inventory dependency: p95 25ms, 0% errors (ev1)."
